  <div class="sec-sub">Insert evaluation with a single line above your function. Automatically measures execution time, tokens, and tool calls, and records TaskResult to PerformanceMonitor.</div>
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">agent_eval</span><span class="kind fn">decorator</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.decorators</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="slbl">Parameters</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">monitor</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>—</td><td>Monitor instance to record results to</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_type</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td>—</td><td>TaskType lowercase string (e.g. <code>"qa"</code>, <code>"tool_use"</code>, <code>"information_retrieval"</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">framework</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">FrameworkLiteral</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Auto-extracts tokens/tools/chain_steps from response objects (24 supported)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_id_prefix</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"task"</code></td><td>Auto-generated task_id prefix</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">question_arg</span> / <span class="p">ground_truth_arg</span> / <span class="p">context_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Remap non-standard function argument names to <code>question</code>/<code>ground_truth</code>/<code>context</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">expected_tools</span> / <span class="p">expected_tools_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[str]|str</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Expected tool list (or arg name to read it from) for Gate F ToolSelectionTracker F1 scoring</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">preset</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Environment-specific config bundle (e.g. <code>"dev"</code>/<code>"staging"</code>/<code>"prod"</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_id_fn</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(args, kwargs) → str</code> dynamic task_id generation</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">flush_every</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Runs save_to_file() automatically every N calls (0=disabled)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">alert_rules</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[SimpleTaskAlertRule]</span></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>List of alert rules to run on task completion</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">rag_mode</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Automatically applies hallucination_detection + <code>information_retrieval</code> task_type</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_hallucination_detection</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Force-enables hallucination detection for this call only</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">security</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">SecurityConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Security 5-metric configuration — <code>SecurityConfig(enable_security_metrics=True)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">llm_judge</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">LLMJudgeConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>LLM Judge configuration — <code>LLMJudgeConfig(model="claude-sonnet-4-6", criteria=["accuracy"])</code>. Included in base install (API key required)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">retry</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">RetryConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Retry policy — <code>RetryConfig(max=3, delay=1.0, backoff=2.0)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">sample_rate</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>1.0</code></td><td>Sampling rate (0–1). For cost control</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">sample_condition</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(args, kwargs) → bool</code> conditional sampling</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">on_record</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(TaskResult) → TaskResult|None</code> post-recording hook</td></tr>
          <tr style="background:var(--bg3)"><td colspan="4" style="font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);padding:6px 10px;font-size:12px">🔧 Harness Engineering Config (v0.8.0+) — 7 Gates · 33 Configs <a href="#harness-a" style="color:var(--text2);font-weight:400;font-size:11px;margin-left:4px">→ Full Reference</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">instructions</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">InstructionConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate A — Instruction compliance, format, keyword validation. <a href="#harness-a" style="color:var(--accent)">→ GoalAlignmentConfig, PlanConfig, and 5 more (6 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">loop_detection</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">LoopDetectionConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate B — Repeated loop detection. <a href="#harness-b" style="color:var(--accent)">→ ScopeConfig, StateConsistencyConfig, DeadlockConfig, and 5 more (6 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">reproducibility</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ReproducibilityConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate C — Reproducibility. <a href="#harness-c" style="color:var(--accent)">→ FaultToleranceConfig, RetryConsistencyConfig, and 4 more (5 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">sla</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">SLAConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate D — SLA response time contract. <a href="#harness-d" style="color:var(--accent)">→ EfficiencyConfig, ResourceBudgetConfig, and 4 more (5 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">threat_severity</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ThreatSeverityConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate E — Threat severity classification. <a href="#harness-e" style="color:var(--accent)">→ ComplianceConfig, ThreatResponseConfig (3 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">consensus</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ConsensusConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate F — Inter-agent consensus rate. <a href="#harness-f" style="color:var(--accent)">→ PropagationConfig, AgentRoleConfig, ConflictResolutionConfig (4 total)</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">explainability</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">ExplainabilityConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Gate G — Reasoning explainability. <a href="#harness-g" style="color:var(--accent)">→ ObservabilityConfig, ErrorDiagnosisConfig, LatencyAttributionConfig (4 total)</a></td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="slbl">Function Signature Rules</div>
      <div class="note tip">💡 Parameters named <code>question</code>·<code>ground_truth</code>·<code>context</code> are auto-recognized. For other names, use <code>question_arg</code>·<code>ground_truth_arg</code>·<code>context_arg</code> to remap.</div>
<pre style="margin-top:10px"><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator</span> <span class="kw">import</span> PerformanceMonitor
<span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.decorators</span> <span class="kw">import</span> agent_eval, EvalMetadata

monitor = <span class="fn">PerformanceMonitor</span>(output_dir=<span class="st">"results/"</span>)

<span class="cm"># basic — execution time and accuracy auto-measured</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">my_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(question)

<span class="cm"># framework auto-extraction (tool_calls, tokens_used, chain_steps)</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"tool_use"</span>, framework=<span class="st">"openai"</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">openai_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>):
    <span class="kw">return</span> client.chat.completions.<span class="fn">create</span>(model=<span class="st">"gpt-4o-mini"</span>, messages=[{<span class="st">"role"</span>:<span class="st">"user"</span>,<span class="st">"content"</span>:question}])

<span class="cm"># return EvalMetadata tuple — manually inject scores, tools, tokens</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"tool_use"</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">tool_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> tuple:
    resp = my_tool.<span class="fn">run</span>(question)
    <span class="kw">return</span> resp, <span class="fn">EvalMetadata</span>(
        tokens_used={<span class="st">"input"</span>: <span class="nm">200</span>, <span class="st">"output"</span>: <span class="nm">150</span>},
        tool_calls=[{<span class="st">"tool"</span>: <span class="st">"search"</span>, <span class="st">"query"</span>: question}],
        expected_tools=[<span class="st">"search"</span>, <span class="st">"calculator"</span>],   <span class="cm"># for F1 calculation</span>
        accuracy_score=<span class="nm">0.95</span>,
    )

<span class="cm"># RAG mode — hallucination_detection auto-enabled</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"information_retrieval"</span>, rag_mode=<span class="kw">True</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">rag_agent</span>(question: str, context: str = <span class="st">""</span>, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> rag.<span class="fn">run</span>(question, context)

<span class="cm"># security mode — temporarily enables 5 trackers incl. InputSanitization, OutputLeakage</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>, security=<span class="fn">SecurityConfig</span>(enable_security_metrics=<span class="kw">True</span>))
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">secure_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> agent.<span class="fn">run</span>(question)

<span class="cm"># LLM Judge + periodic save combination</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>,
             llm_judge=<span class="fn">LLMJudgeConfig</span>(model=<span class="st">"claude-sonnet-4-6"</span>),
             flush_every=<span class="nm">50</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">prod_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(question)

<span class="cm"># async functions natively supported</span>
<span class="de">@agent_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>)
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">async_agent</span>(question: str, ground_truth: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return await</span> llm.<span class="fn">ainvoke</span>(question)</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── @batch_eval ── -->
<section class="sec" id="batch-eval">
  <div class="sec-title">📦 @batch_eval <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text2);margin-left:8px">v0.7.1+ · Batch Evaluation</span></div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Evaluates multiple tasks at once from a list input. Each item is recorded as an independent TaskResult.</div>
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">batch_eval</span><span class="kind fn">decorator</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.decorators</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="slbl">Parameters</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">monitor</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>—</td><td>Monitor instance to record results to (pass a List to record to multiple monitors simultaneously)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_type</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"qa"</code></td><td>TaskType lowercase string</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">questions_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"questions"</code></td><td>Function parameter name holding the question list</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">ground_truths_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"ground_truths"</code></td><td>Function parameter name holding the ground truth list</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">framework</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">FrameworkLiteral</span></td><td><code>"native"</code></td><td>Auto-extracts metadata from 24 frameworks</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">concurrency</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Max parallel execution per item (asyncio.gather). 0=sequential</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">item_timeout</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Per-item timeout (seconds)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">on_item_error</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(exception, item_idx) → None</code> per-item error handling callback</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">return_format</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"list"</code></td><td><code>"list"</code> | <code>"tuple"</code> | <code>"dataframe"</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">flush_every</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Runs save_to_file() automatically every N batch calls</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">alert_rules</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[SimpleTaskAlertRule]</span></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Alert rule list</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">llm_judge</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">LLMJudgeConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Apply LLM Judge to entire batch — <code>LLMJudgeConfig(model=..., criteria=[...])</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">security</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">SecurityConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Security 5-metric configuration — <code>SecurityConfig(enable_security_metrics=True)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">on_batch_complete</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(results: list) → None</code> hook after batch completes</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="note tip" style="margin-top:8px">💡 Function signature: <code>(questions: list, ground_truths: list = None) → list</code>. Return list and input list are index-aligned 1:1. Use <code>questions_arg</code>/<code>ground_truths_arg</code> to remap parameter names.</div>
<pre style="margin-top:10px"><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.decorators</span> <span class="kw">import</span> batch_eval

<span class="cm"># basic batch evaluation</span>
<span class="de">@batch_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>, flush_every=<span class="nm">20</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">batch_agent</span>(questions: list, ground_truths: list = <span class="kw">None</span>) -> list:
    <span class="kw">return</span> [llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(q) <span class="kw">for</span> q <span class="kw">in</span> questions]

batch_agent(
    questions=[<span class="st">"Q1"</span>, <span class="st">"Q2"</span>, <span class="st">"Q3"</span>],
    ground_truths=[<span class="st">"A1"</span>, <span class="st">"A2"</span>, <span class="st">"A3"</span>],
)

<span class="cm"># parallel processing — concurrency=8 cap (asyncio.gather)</span>
<span class="de">@batch_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>, concurrency=<span class="nm">8</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">parallel_agent</span>(questions: list, ground_truths: list = <span class="kw">None</span>) -> list:
    <span class="kw">return</span> [llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(q) <span class="kw">for</span> q <span class="kw">in</span> questions]

<span class="cm"># DataFrame return (includes task_id, accuracy_score, completion_score, tokens_total ...)</span>
<span class="de">@batch_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"tool_use"</span>, return_format=<span class="st">"dataframe"</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">df_agent</span>(questions: list, ground_truths: list = <span class="kw">None</span>) -> list:
    <span class="kw">return</span> [agent.<span class="fn">run</span>(q) <span class="kw">for</span> q <span class="kw">in</span> questions]

df = <span class="fn">df_agent</span>(questions=[...], ground_truths=[...])
<span class="cm"># df.columns → ['task_id', 'task_type', 'success', 'accuracy_score', ...]</span>

<span class="cm"># error callback + per-item timeout</span>
<span class="de">@batch_eval</span>(monitor, task_type=<span class="st">"qa"</span>,
             on_item_error=<span class="kw">lambda</span> exc, idx: <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"[ERR] item {idx}: {exc}"</span>),
             item_timeout=<span class="nm">30.0</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">robust_agent</span>(questions: list, ground_truths: list = <span class="kw">None</span>) -> list:
    <span class="kw">return</span> [risky_call(q) <span class="kw">for</span> q <span class="kw">in</span> questions]</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── @conversation_eval ── -->
<section class="sec" id="conversation-eval">
  <div class="sec-title">💬 @conversation_eval <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text2);margin-left:8px">v0.7.1+ · Multi-turn Conversation</span></div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Evaluates multi-turn conversations at the session level. Calling with the same <code>session_id</code> automatically accumulates turns and records <code>ConversationMetrics</code> when the session ends.</div>
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">conversation_eval</span><span class="kind fn">decorator</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.decorators</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="slbl">Parameters</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">monitor</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>—</td><td>Monitor instance to record results to</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">session_id_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"session_id"</code></td><td>Function parameter name holding the session ID. Auto-recognized if the function has <code>session_id: str</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">user_arg</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"question"</code></td><td>Function parameter name holding the user utterance</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">max_turns</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Maximum number of turns per session</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">max_turns_exceeded_action</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"flush"</code></td><td><code>"flush"</code> | <code>"warn"</code> | <code>"error"</code> — action when max turns exceeded</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">max_session_seconds</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Inactive session auto-flush timer (seconds)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">flush_every</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>0</code></td><td>Runs save_to_file() automatically every N sessions</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">on_turn</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(session_id, user, response, metadata) → None</code> turn-complete hook</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">on_flush</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(metrics, session_id) → None</code> session flush-complete hook</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">session_score_fn</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Callable</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td><code>(ConversationMetrics) → float</code> custom session score</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">llm_judge</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">LLMJudgeConfig</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Apply LLM Judge per session</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="slbl">ConversationMetrics — Auto-calculated Metrics</div>
      <table class="mtable" style="margin-bottom:10px">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Range</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="p">turn_count</span></td><td><span class="r">int</span></td><td>Total conversation turns</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">context_retention_score</span></td><td><span class="r">0–1</span></td><td>Prior utterance information retention rate</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">topic_coherence_score</span></td><td><span class="r">0–1</span></td><td>Conversation topic coherence</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">progressive_depth_score</span></td><td><span class="r">0–1</span></td><td>Conversation depth progression</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">session_completion_score</span></td><td><span class="r">0–1</span></td><td>Session completion (response length-based)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">overall_score</span></td><td><span class="r">0–1</span></td><td>Weighted average of 4 dimensions</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">avg_turn_latency</span></td><td><span class="r">float</span></td><td>Average response time per turn (seconds)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
<pre><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.decorators</span> <span class="kw">import</span> conversation_eval

<span class="cm"># basic — auto session separation by session_id parameter</span>
<span class="de">@conversation_eval</span>(monitor, flush_every=<span class="nm">10</span>)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">chat_agent</span>(user_input: str, session_id: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(user_input)

<span class="cm"># calling with same session_id → auto multi-turn accumulation</span>
chat_agent(<span class="st">"Hello!"</span>, session_id=<span class="st">"user_001"</span>)
chat_agent(<span class="st">"How's the weather today?"</span>, session_id=<span class="st">"user_001"</span>)
chat_agent(<span class="st">"Then suggest some weekend plans"</span>, session_id=<span class="st">"user_001"</span>)
<span class="cm"># → context_retention, topic_coherence, progressive_depth auto-aggregated</span>

<span class="cm"># different user → separate session</span>
chat_agent(<span class="st">"I want to learn Python"</span>, session_id=<span class="st">"user_002"</span>)
chat_agent(<span class="st">"Where do I start?"</span>, session_id=<span class="st">"user_002"</span>)

<span class="cm"># custom score function + turn-complete hook</span>
<span class="de">@conversation_eval</span>(
    monitor,
    session_score_fn=<span class="kw">lambda</span> m: (m.context_retention_score + m.topic_coherence_score) / <span class="nm">2</span>,
    on_turn=<span class="kw">lambda</span> sid, idx, u, r: <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"[Turn {idx}] {sid}: {r[:50]}"</span>),
    max_turns=<span class="nm">20</span>, max_turns_exceeded_action=<span class="st">"flush"</span>,
)
<span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">monitored_chat</span>(user_input: str, session_id: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return</span> llm.<span class="fn">invoke</span>(user_input)

<span class="cm"># async support</span>
<span class="de">@conversation_eval</span>(monitor)
<span class="kw">async def</span> <span class="fn">async_chat</span>(user_input: str, session_id: str = <span class="st">""</span>) -> str:
    <span class="kw">return await</span> llm.<span class="fn">ainvoke</span>(user_input)</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── eval_context ── -->
<section class="sec" id="eval-context">
  <div class="sec-title">🔄 eval_context <span style="font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text2);margin-left:8px">v0.7.2+ · Inline Evaluation</span></div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Evaluate external function calls using a <code>with</code> block. Ideal for third-party code where applying a decorator is difficult, or for interactive testing.</div>
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head"><span class="cls-name">eval_context</span><span class="kind ctx">@contextmanager</span><span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.decorators</span></div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="slbl">Parameters</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">monitor</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>—</td><td>Monitor instance to record results to</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_type</span><span class="req">✦</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td>—</td><td>TaskType lowercase string</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">question</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>""</code></td><td>Question being evaluated</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">ground_truth</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>""</code></td><td>Ground truth</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">task_id</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td>auto</td><td>Task ID (auto-generated UUID if not specified)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">timeout</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Block timeout (seconds)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">alert_rules</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[SimpleTaskAlertRule]</span></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>List of alert rules</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="note" style="margin-top:8px">🔧 Assign the response to <code>ctx.response</code> — TaskResult is recorded automatically when the block exits. Record streaming chunks with <code>ctx.chunk_step(chunk)</code>.</div>
<pre style="margin-top:10px"><span class="kw">from</span> <span class="cn">agent_evaluator.decorators</span> <span class="kw">import</span> eval_context

<span class="cm"># basic usage — assign external function result to ctx.response</span>
<span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">eval_context</span>(monitor, <span class="st">"qa"</span>,
                  question=<span class="st">"What is the capital of France?"</span>,
                  ground_truth=<span class="st">"Paris"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> ctx:
    ctx.response = third_party_llm.<span class="fn">ask</span>(<span class="st">"What is the capital of France?"</span>)
<span class="cm"># block exits → execution time and accuracy auto-recorded</span>

<span class="cm"># streaming — TTFT auto-recorded via chunk_step()</span>
<span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">eval_context</span>(monitor, <span class="st">"qa"</span>, question=<span class="st">"Explain this"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> ctx:
    chunks = []
    <span class="kw">for</span> chunk <span class="kw">in</span> streaming_llm.<span class="fn">stream</span>(<span class="st">"Explain this"</span>):
        chunks.<span class="fn">append</span>(chunk)
        ctx.<span class="fn">chunk_step</span>(chunk)   <span class="cm"># first chunk → TTFT auto-recorded</span>
    ctx.response = <span class="st">""</span>.<span class="fn">join</span>(chunks)

<span class="cm"># nested context (depth tracked via ctx.depth)</span>
<span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">eval_context</span>(monitor, <span class="st">"tool_use"</span>, question=<span class="st">"complex task"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> outer:
    <span class="kw">with</span> <span class="fn">eval_context</span>(monitor, <span class="st">"qa"</span>, question=<span class="st">"subtask"</span>) <span class="kw">as</span> inner:
        inner.response = sub_agent.<span class="fn">run</span>(<span class="st">"subtask"</span>)
    outer.response = main_agent.<span class="fn">run</span>(<span class="st">"complex task"</span>)</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ── PerformanceMonitor ── -->
<section class="sec" id="performance-monitor">
  <div class="sec-title">🎛️ PerformanceMonitor</div>
  <div class="sec-sub">Central orchestrator coordinating 16 Layer 1+2 trackers internally. The core class called internally by decorators.</div>
  <div class="cls-card">
    <div class="cls-head">
      <span class="cls-name">PerformanceMonitor</span><span class="kind cls">class</span>
      <span class="cls-src">agent_evaluator.core.trackers.monitor</span>
    </div>
    <div class="cls-body">
      <div class="slbl">Constructor Parameters</div>
      {% call param_table() %}
          <tr><td><span class="p">output_dir</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>"results/"</code></td><td>JSON/HTML report save directory</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">pricing</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Dict[str,float]</span></td><td><code>{"input":0.003,"output":0.015}</code></td><td>Cost per 1K tokens (USD). Passed to TokenEconomyTracker.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">model_name</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>""</code></td><td>Model name used for this evaluation (e.g. <code>"claude-sonnet-4-5"</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">session_label</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str</span></td><td><code>""</code></td><td>Free-text label for this monitor session (dashboard display)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_hallucination_detection</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Activates HallucinationDetector (incurs LLM call cost)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_security_metrics</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Activates 5 Layer 2 security trackers</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">security_config</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">Dict</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>ToolAuthorizationTracker configuration (allowed_tools, restricted_tools, etc.)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enabled_security_trackers</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[str]|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Selectively enable specific security trackers (only valid when <code>enable_security_metrics=True</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_llm_judge</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Activates LLM-as-Judge automatic scoring. Automatically applies 5 dimensions (completeness, relevance, factual consistency, toxicity, bias).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_model</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Judge model. None → auto-detects from <code>agent-eval init</code> configuration.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_sample_rate</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>0.1</code></td><td>Judge evaluation rate (0.0–1.0). For cost control.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_budget_per_day</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Daily Judge budget cap (USD). Skips judging when exceeded.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_criteria</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[str]|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>G-Eval custom evaluation criteria list (DeepEval alternative). e.g. <code>["medical_accuracy", "empathy"]</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_escalation_model</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">str|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>v0.8.3+ — auto re-scores with a stronger model when the primary judge score falls below <code>judge_escalation_threshold</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">judge_seed</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Sampling seed for reproducible judge sampling</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">use_korean_tokenizer</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Korean morphological tokenization (requires <code>kiwipiepy</code>)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">use_semantic_hallucination</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Embedding-based semantic hallucination detection (requires <code>sentence-transformers</code>, opt-in)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_anomaly_detection</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Runs AnomalyDetector.scan() automatically on save_to_file(). Results stored in anomaly_data.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">anomaly_baseline_window</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>100</code></td><td>Maximum tasks to use for baseline calculation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">anomaly_detection_window</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>20</code></td><td>Recent tasks to use for current state comparison.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">auto_save</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Automatically calls <code>save_to_file()</code> every <code>auto_save_interval</code> calls to <code>record_task()</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_transparency</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>Activates TestTransparencyManager</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">gate_a_tcr_weight</span> / <span class="p">gate_c_tcr_weight</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>0.4</code></td><td>Relative weight of the TCR component vs. remaining Config metrics in Gate A/C scoring (0.0–1.0)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">gate_b_loop_weight</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">float</span></td><td><code>0.0</code></td><td>Loop-detection weight in Gate B (<code>0.0</code> = simple average of available metrics)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">min_samples_default</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>3</code></td><td>SPEC-002 — shared minimum-sample-size guard threshold across all Gates A–G</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">retention_mode</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">"full"|"windowed"</span></td><td><code>"full"</code></td><td>SPEC-004 — <code>"windowed"</code> caps <code>self.tasks</code> to <code>window_size</code> while still reflecting full history for Gate running aggregates (SPEC-018)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">window_size</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">int</span></td><td><code>10000</code></td><td>Task window size when <code>retention_mode="windowed"</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">storage_backend</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">"json"|"sqlite"</span></td><td><code>"json"</code></td><td>SPEC-016 — <code>"sqlite"</code> upserts by <code>task_id</code> instead of rewriting the whole file on every <code>save_to_file()</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">enable_pii_redaction</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">bool</span></td><td><code>False</code></td><td>SPEC-020 — masks PII in <code>question</code>/<code>response</code>/<code>context</code>/<code>ground_truth</code> at <code>save_to_file()</code> time only (in-memory data untouched)</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">pii_redaction_categories</span><span class="opt">opt</span></td><td><span class="t">List[str]|None</span></td><td><code>None</code></td><td>Restrict PII redaction to specific categories (default: all supported categories)</td></tr>
      {% endcall %}
      <div class="slbl">Key Methods</div>
      <table class="mtable">
        <thead><tr><th>Method Signature</th><th>Return</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><span class="p">record_task(result, ground_truth=None, context=None, request=None, response=None, expected_elements=None)</span></td><td><span class="r">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>Records TaskResult to all active trackers. Returns <code>self</code> for method chaining.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">generate_report(force_recompute=False)</span></td><td><span class="r">EvaluationReport</span></td><td>Aggregates collected data and returns an EvaluationReport object. SPEC-014 — cached and skipped when nothing new has been recorded, unless <code>force_recompute=True</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">save_to_file(filename)</span></td><td><span class="r">str</span></td><td>Saves <code>{output_dir}/{filename}.json</code> + <code>.html</code> (or <code>.db</code> when <code>storage_backend="sqlite"</code>). Returns the saved path. Automatically includes anomaly_data when <code>enable_anomaly_detection=True</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">conversation(session_id, task_type="qa")</span></td><td><span class="r">ConversationSession</span></td><td>Multi-turn conversation evaluation context manager. <code>with monitor.conversation("id") as conv: conv.turn(user=..., agent=...)</code></td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">record_implicit_feedback(task_id, event_type, value=None)</span></td><td><span class="r">None</span></td><td>Records user reaction signals (like/copy/retry/share) → stored in feedback_data</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">evaluate_with_golden_dataset(agent_fn, dataset_path=None, ...)</span></td><td><span class="r">Dict</span></td><td>Auto-evaluates agent with golden dataset</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">compare_with_thresholds()</span></td><td><span class="r">Dict</span></td><td>Compares current metrics with industry thresholds</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">reset(keep_config=True)</span></td><td><span class="r">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>Clears all accumulated tracker data (thread-safe). Returns <code>self</code>. <code>keep_config=True</code> preserves constructor settings (pricing, judge config, etc.) while clearing recorded tasks.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">invalidate_report_cache()</span></td><td><span class="r">None</span></td><td>SPEC-014 — manually marks the cached report stale. Required after any in-place <code>TaskResult</code> mutation that bypasses <code>record_task()</code>.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">for_rag_evaluation(**kwargs)</span></td><td><span class="r">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>classmethod. Automatically applies optimal RAG evaluation settings (<code>enable_hallucination_detection=True</code>).</td></tr>
          <tr><td><span class="p">for_secure_agents(**kwargs)</span></td><td><span class="r">PerformanceMonitor</span></td><td>classmethod. Automatically applies optimal security evaluation settings (<code>enable_security_metrics=True</code>).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <div class="note tip" style="margin-top:12px">💡 <strong>Relationship with decorators</strong>: <code>@agent_eval</code>, <code>@batch_eval</code>, and <code>eval_context</code> all call <code>monitor.record_task()</code> internally. Direct calls are only needed for advanced usage.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

